{"id": "EUVD-2026-91435", "enisaUuid": "173c3249-1685-38f6-a7af-7eba313c11c8", "description": "Zebra before 6.1.0 contains an incorrect calculation vulnerability in its ZIP-317 block template selector that omits header and transaction-count size from the block budget. Attackers can place valid selectable transactions in a victim miner's mempool to shape templates into oversized blocks, causing rejection and wasted proof-of-work.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T02:38:24", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/security/advisories/GHSA-95m2-vx53-v2jw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zebra-before-6.1.0-incorrect-block-size-calculation-in-getblocktemplate"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104424", "GHSA-3xx8-299f-8q53"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "69f53aa6-2bce-372a-b6f1-7eb43838c6c8", "product": {"name": "zebra", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a4e1c375-f497-3da4-b62e-021dd221f533", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}], "isExploited": false}